<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Talents Around Us – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Talents Around Us</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Will Play the Drums in the Parade.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Edit short texts with peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write short descriptive paragraphs about preparing for Fiestas Patrias celebrations (e.g., 'If I practice the traditional dance every day, I will perform well in the parade.' 'I will wear my pollera during the school celebration.').</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can write coherent, simple descriptive texts about Fiestas Patrias events (e.g., 'First, the honor roll student will carry the Panamanian flag, then the school band will play, and finally, the dancers will perform traditional dances.').</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can edit and revise short descriptions of Fiestas Patrias activities with peers, adding details and suggestions (e.g., 'Let's add more information about the parade, like who will carry the Panamanian flag and what songs the band will play.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 55%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 10%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of the lesson's main topic and linguistic content.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various pictures of Fiestas Patrias parades, featuring students playing instruments (drums, flute, accordion), dancing traditional dances, and carrying the Panamanian flag. Students orally brainstorm words related to what they see (e.g., 'parade', 'flag', 'band', 'costume', 'dance', 'performer', 'music', 'talent', 'excited'). The teacher writes these words on the board, ensuring key vocabulary from the theme is covered.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models short sentences about parade plans, demonstrating correct pronunciation and simple sentence structure. For example, "I can play the flute." "If I practice my dance, I will perform well." "We will wear colorful costumes for the celebration." The teacher points out the future simple tense ('will') and the first conditional structure ('If... will...'), and the modal 'can'. Attention is also given to the pronunciation of minimal pairs like /ʌ/ in 'fun' and /æ/ in 'band' when using words like 'drums' and 'band' in sentences.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say, 'I will march in the parade,' am I marching now or in the future?" (Expected answer: In the future.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can a person who sings well be called a 'performer'?" (Expected answer: Yes.)</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to the Scenario: "The Talents Around Us."</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive text (1-2 paragraphs) from a fictional 6th-grade student about their plans and preparation for the Fiestas Patrias parade. The text includes examples of future simple, first conditional, and the modal 'can', and integrates the target vocabulary. Genre: descriptive narrative, Register: informal/personal, Format: short paragraph.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example Text:</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; font-style: italic;">"Hi, I'm Sofia! I am very excited for Panama's National Holidays. I can play the accordion, and I will perform a traditional Panamanian song in the school parade. If I practice every day, I will play beautifully. First, the honor roll student will carry the Panamanian flag. Then, our school band will march, and finally, my friend Miguel will play the drums. We will all wear our colorful costumes! It will be an amazing event."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpret and produce short written texts for various purposes and audiences.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the text silently.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Activity:</b> The teacher reads statements about the text, and students indicate True or False (e.g., "Sofia will play the flute." - False; "Sofia can play the accordion." - True; "The honor roll student will carry the flag first." - True).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Check:</b> Students underline all verbs related to performing (e.g., 'play', 'perform', 'march') and circle all adjectives (e.g., 'excited', 'beautifully', 'colorful', 'amazing').</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing. Students practice the target language in controlled and semi-controlled activities.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using the future simple tense for plans, the first conditional for real possibilities, and the modal 'can' to express ability or talent, incorporating vocabulary related to Fiestas Patrias celebrations.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher provides sentences with blanks. Students complete them using the correct form of 'will', 'can', or 'if... will...' and appropriate vocabulary.
                    <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">I _____ (play) the drums in the parade. (will play)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">If I _____ (practice) my dance, I _____ (perform) well. (practice, will perform)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">My friend _____ (sing) a patriotic song. (will sing)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">She _____ (twirl) the baton. (can twirl)</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Creation (Semi-Controlled Practice):</b> Students use given prompts and target grammar structures to write original sentences about Fiestas Patrias events or talents.
                    <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt: (Your talent) + (what you will do) -> Example: "I can dance. I will perform a traditional dance."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt: (Practice) + (Result) -> Example: "If I rehearse my song, I will sing beautifully."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt: (A friend's plan) -> Example: "My friend will play the flute in the band."</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Sentence Check:</b> Students work in pairs. Each student writes 3-4 original sentences about their talents or plans for the parade, using 'will', 'can', and 'if... will...'. They then exchange their sentences with their partner. Partners read and gently circle any potential errors in grammar, spelling, or vocabulary. They also check for distinguishing rhyming words from non-rhyming words used in sentences (e.g., 'drum' and 'hum').</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Talents Around Us."</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Written Product & Peer Editing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Task: "Our Fiestas Patrias Parade Plan"</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Individual Writing (10 min):</b> Each student writes a short descriptive paragraph (4-6 sentences) about their role or a fictional role in the upcoming Fiestas Patrias parade. The paragraph must include:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two sentences using the future simple tense (e.g., "I will play the drums." "My class will march first.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one sentence using the first conditional (e.g., "If I practice my song, I will perform well.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one sentence using the modal 'can' to express ability (e.g., "I can dance traditional dances.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Vocabulary from the theme (e.g., 'costume', 'band', 'parade', 'talented', 'celebrate').</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Editing (8 min):</b> Students exchange their written paragraphs with a partner. They respectfully collaborate to edit and revise each other's texts. Partners should:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Check for correct use of 'will', 'can', and 'if... will...' grammar structures.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify and correct spelling errors, focusing on distinguishing rhyming words related to the theme (e.g., 'drum' and 'hum' versus 'flag' and 'march').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggest adding more descriptive details or clarifying information to make the text more engaging (e.g., "Can you add more information about your costume?" "Let's add what song the band will play.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use polite language for suggestions (e.g., "Maybe you can add...", "How about we say...?").</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Revision (2 min):</b> Students take back their paragraphs and make final revisions based on their partner's feedback.</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">20 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation during peer editing and collection of revised written paragraphs. Peer assessment rubric focusing on criteria below.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their final, revised descriptive paragraphs about their Fiestas Patrias parade plans and talents.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer):</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Grammar:</b> Correct use of future simple, first conditional, and modal 'can' (A2.1).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Integration of at least 5-7 theme-related vocabulary words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Cohesion and Clarity:</b> The paragraph is simple, coherent, and easy to understand.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Editing & Revision:</b> Evidence of peer suggestions and revisions incorporated into the final text.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Spelling and Punctuation:</b> Minimizes common errors appropriate for A2.1 level.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you learned or improved in your writing today?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most helpful suggestion your partner gave you?"</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">7-8 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection on the lesson's effectiveness and future planning.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy about writing about Fiestas Patrias plans today? What was difficult?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did working with a partner help you make your writing better?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
            <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students successfully edit short texts with peers? Were the suggestions detailed and polite?</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were students able to consistently apply future simple, first conditional, and 'can' in their writing? Which grammar point needs more review?</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments are needed for the next writing task or for students who struggled with forming coherent sentences? (e.g., providing more sentence starters or a checklist for peer editing).</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In our next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration), we will use these edited descriptive paragraphs to create a collaborative "Fiestas Patrias Talent Show Program" or a "Parade Line-up" document, consolidating our talents and plans for the upcoming celebration.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
    </tr>
</table>